00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:24.780
Beautiful, although not the most glamorous
town, but are still pretty good.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:25.780
That's good.

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:32.180
Um, I have a question about COVID restrictions,
especially in the post vaccine world.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:33.180
Yeah.

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:39.690
So countries like the UK and Australia, what
we've done is once the majority of the population

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:41.960
is vaccinated, especially older people.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:46.060
Yes, we've kind of had to let it rip approach.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:51.130
And obviously, it's very different in the
US because of the kind of political situation

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:53.220
and the decentralized system there.

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:57.579
But here in the UK, yeah, a bit of a let let
it rip approach.

00:00:57.579 --> 00:01:00.670
And I'm not the biggest fan of Boris Johnson.

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:06.439
There's lots of things to criticize him for,
but I think this is one thing that he's got

00:01:06.439 --> 00:01:07.439
right.

00:01:07.439 --> 00:01:11.649
In the case where you put your faith in the
vaccines and then you, yeah, you open up the

00:01:11.649 --> 00:01:15.060
economy and you basically let the virus do
its thing.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:22.049
And I think my my understanding is on balance
when you balance health, economy, et cetera,

00:01:22.049 --> 00:01:23.219
I think that's the right thing.

00:01:23.219 --> 00:01:26.109
Did you but did you have an opinion on this
approach?

00:01:26.109 --> 00:01:31.529
Do you think it's better to be more cautious
or kind of just let things happen?

00:01:31.529 --> 00:01:35.569
Speaker 1: The answer is different depending
on what is happening.

00:01:35.569 --> 00:01:41.670
At the time, there was a moment where the
vaccines were very good at preventing people

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:44.889
from getting sick at all.

00:01:44.889 --> 00:01:50.119
But now we have a situation where the vaccines
are better at preventing people from getting

00:01:50.119 --> 00:01:52.539
seriously ill and dying on average.

00:01:52.539 --> 00:01:59.049
Remember on average, and the virus is now
so transmissible that there really is no containing

00:01:59.049 --> 00:02:00.049
it.

00:02:00.049 --> 00:02:03.869
So I think the right approach changes as the
circumstances on the ground change.

00:02:03.869 --> 00:02:08.780
Now, as far as the UK moving in the direction
of removing all COVID restrictions, including

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:13.290
masking, which remind me, is it in 60 days
that that's happening or when is that happening?

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:16.370
Speaker 4: That is now happening in about
10

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:17.930
Speaker 1: days, in about 10 days.

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:18.930
OK.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:22.770
When it comes to that, when you look at, you
know, you guys are ahead of the U.S. in terms

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:26.260
of the immigrant wave, you're already well
on the decline.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:31.990
If you believe that at this point it is becoming
endemic, that Macron has burned through the

00:02:31.990 --> 00:02:37.640
population and at least until next flu season,
things are going to be well controlled.

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:43.290
It doesn't seem crazy to me to say, Listen,
the vaccines have been available for a year.

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:47.910
We have a less severe but very contagious
variant, which is still more serious than

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:51.560
a cold, but much less serious than the previous
ones.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:58.150
If we can keep the medical system from being
overwhelmed while removing restrictions at

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:02.150
a certain point, I understand that countries
are going to do it and it doesn't seem crazy

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:06.250
now if in the fall there's a much more deadly
variant.

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:12.710
And there's a different situation, my opinion
might change, but the numbers point to me

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:15.950
understanding why the U.K. is doing what it's
doing now.

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:21.790
Speaker 4: Yeah, I agree, and I think it's
a good gamble politically as well, because

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:26.950
